 ## 4. Domain model (the fee decision)
 
-One concept drives everything: per signed guest, a **fee decision** that resolves to
-exactly one of three outcomes.
+For each signed guest and each period, `stay_fee.guest_period` returns exactly one status:
 
-| Outcome | When | Liable nights | Exempt nights |
+| Status | When | Liable nights | Exempt nights |
 |---|---|---|---|
-| **liable** | signed, adult on arrival, stay â‰¤ 60 days, no host override | `nights` | 0 |
-| **exempt** | under 18 on arrival, OR host set `fee_host_decision = 'exempt'` | 0 | `nights` |
-| **not subject** | stay > 60 days (Â§3a) | 0 | 0 (not counted at all) |
+| **not_subject** | the whole stay is `nights + 1 > 60` (Â§3a). Checked **first**; no decision changes it | 0 | 0 (not reported at all) |
+| **exempt** | host `exempt` (reason required), **or** under 18 on the arrival day with no host decision | 0 | nights in period |
+| **liable** | otherwise, including host `charge` (corrects a wrong birth date) | nights in period | 0 |
 
-A host **charge** override (`fee_host_decision = 'charge'`) forces *liable* even for
-a minor (e.g. an adult booking for a child). The automatic rules handle under-18 and
-over-60; every other Â§3b exemption (ZTP/P, blind, dependent, local resident, etc.)
-is a host decision with a stored reason. There is **no guest-facing input** â€” see Â§7.
+A guest's decision applies to the whole stay, in every period it touches.
 
